    "answer_baseline": "Based on the provided context:\n\n* **Wholly State-Funded Institutions:** No religious instruction shall be provided in any educational institution that is wholly maintained out of State funds [Article 28(1)].\n* **Exception for Trusts/Endowments:** Religious instruction is permitted in an institution administered by the State if it was established under an endowment or trust that requires such instruction to be imparted [Article 28(2)].\n* **State-Aided Institutions:** In educational institutions receiving aid out of State funds, religious instruction may be imparted, but no person attending can be required to take part in any religious instruction or attend religious worship unless they (or their guardian, if a minor) give consent [Article 28(3)].",
    "answer_reranked": "Based on the provided context, the rules regarding religious instruction in government-funded or State-administered educational institutions are as follows:\n\n* **Institutions wholly maintained out of State funds:** No religious instruction shall be provided in any educational institution that is wholly maintained out of State funds (Article 28(1)).\n* **State-administered institutions under an endowment or trust:** Religious instruction is permitted in an educational institution administered by the State if it was established under any endowment or trust requiring that religious instruction be imparted in it (Article 28(2)).\n* **Institutions receiving aid out of State funds:** In educational institutions receiving aid out of State funds (or recognized by the State), religious instruction may take place, but no person attending can be required to participate in any religious instruction or attend religious worship unless that person—or their guardian, if they are a minor—has given consent (Article 28(3))."
